From e6bf3bce7d4e221a405886ebe8b085e5fe860e5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Brian S. Park" <brianspark@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:20:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] mmvq: 32-element dense Q4_K dot product on gfx1100
 (RDNA3_0), one integer chain per sub-block

On gfx1100 the multi-row Q4_K verify kernel (4 rows x ncols_dst columns per
wave, VDR 2) is instruction-bound: per 16 weights and (row, column) it pays
two scale multiplies, two converts and two fmas, plus the scale/min unpack
per row, around 4 dot4 per (row, column).

vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4_dense takes 32 elements per call (VDR 4).  Its two
16-element chunks belong to the same two sub-blocks, so each sub-block's 16
products are summed in one integer dp4a chain before the single
scale/convert/fma (|dot1| <= 16*15*127, times the 6-bit scale < 2^21:
exact); the mins term keeps the exact-product form and the scale words are
packed as in vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1.  RDNA3_0 dense Q4_K only (MoE keeps
vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_vdr4, other arches vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1).

get_vdr_mmvq_dense() is the one VDR the dense kernels and the host-side K
split both read, so they agree on the RDNA3_0 override.

Output: the K partition changes, so greedy text differs from the parent
once; single-token decode and every verify width share the dot product, so
widths stay bit-identical (model logits width probe PASS at P = 256 and
3584; MTP text == plain text).

gfx1100 W = 4 hot loop: 599 instructions per 32 elements (was 475 per 16),
VGPR 94 -> 118, 0 scratch.  rocprofv3, one MTP request, Q4_K W = 4 kernels:
ffn_gate/up 75.0 -> 71.2 us, 5120-row 44.0 -> 40.0, attn_gate 29.1 -> 27.4,
attn_qkv 44.0 -> 41.9, attn_q 49.6 -> 48.3; W = 1 fused gate/up 120 -> 117.

Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M, MTP draft 3, means of 4 runs x 2 requests vs parent:
  MTP code   84.10 -> 87.23 t/s (+3.7 %, same text and acceptance)
  MTP prose  70.75 -> 73.95 (+4.5 %; acceptance 0.666 -> 0.672)
  MTP @ 26k  56.33 -> 59.94 (+6.4 %; acceptance 0.638 -> 0.668)
  plain      37.77 -> 38.50 (+1.9 %)

